<header class="page-masthead"><div class="wrap masthead-inner"><h1>About</h1><p>My work centres on inequality, development governance and public policy, with a particular interest in East and Southeast Asia. I examine how political institutions shape household living standards and access to public protection.</p></div></header>
<p class="wrap profile-name">I publish as Ashton Milton. My full name is Ashton Kyle Milton.</p>
<div class="wrap about-reading editorial-copy"><p>I study Politics and Sociology at Queen Mary University of London and completed a year abroad at Waseda University’s School of Political Science and Economics in Tokyo. My background includes journalism, hospitality operations, community research and educational governance.</p><p>Living in Tokyo encouraged me to write about the public systems I encountered each day, from commuter rail to neighbourhood maintenance. Those observations continue to inform my essays on cities and everyday life.</p><h2>Education</h2><h3>Queen Mary University of London</h3><p>BA Politics and Sociology with Year Abroad · 2023–2027 (final-year undergraduate)</p><h3>Waseda University, Tokyo</h3><p>School of Political Science and Economics · 2025–2026 (completed year abroad)</p><h2>Research and Governance</h2><p>My dissertation, Rising Powers, Unequal Lives, compares the roles of earnings and redistribution in household income gains in China and Vietnam between 2010 and 2025. I am developing a qualitative comparison of the income patterns and the political incentives and financing arrangements that might explain them.</p><h3>London Living Wage Research Project</h3><p>Citizens UK and Queen Mary University of London · 2024</p><p>I contributed to research on the London Living Wage in Tower Hamlets as part of a university project linked to a community campaign.</p><h3>Capital City College Group</h3><p>Board member · November 2020–June 2022</p><p>As a student board member, I contributed to discussions of educational quality, institutional strategy and the learner experience.</p><a class="button" href="/research/">Research Outline</a><h2>Journalism</h2><h3>Luxuriate Life Magazine</h3><p>Lifestyle journalist · June–December 2023</p><p>My features covered travel, gastronomy, fashion and consumer culture. The role involved researching and writing for print and digital publication to editorial briefs and deadlines.</p><h3>Newsquest Media Group</h3><p>Reporter · October 2020–March 2021</p><p>At Newsquest, I researched local stories and conducted interviews, working with regional editors on news and features.</p><h2>Operations and Management</h2><h3>Gouqi London</h3><p>Reservations, sales and systems manager · January 2023–September 2023</p><p>My role combined reservations and guest communications with responsibility for booking systems and coordination across management, reception and service teams.</p><h3>Lantana</h3><p>Floor and reception supervisor · August–December 2022</p><p>My work included supporting a new venue launch, staff training and daily front-of-house coordination.</p><h2>Skills and Languages</h2><p>My experience includes documentary research, interviewing, source evaluation and qualitative policy analysis. I write for both academic and editorial audiences.</p><p>Languages: English (native) · French (intermediate) · Japanese (beginner)</p><a class="button" href="/writing/">Work Archive</a></div>
